<title>GERMANY: German metals production generally up in Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>German metals production generally up in Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German metals production in the first 10 months of 1996 was generally higher than in the same 1995 period, monthly data from state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Only refined lead was substantially down, a 24.8 percent drop against January/October 1995. Lead castings were up against last year but not as strongly as in earlier months.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes--  METALS OUTPUT	   Oct 96   Jan/Oct 96	 pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/Oct 95</p>
<p> primary aluminium     48,633     480,169		 +  0.7</p>
<p> electrolytic copper   51,465     495,087		 + 12.0</p>
<p> zinc			27,656     273,848		 +  1.9</p>
<p> refined lead	    18,136     147,754		 - 24.8</p>
<p> SEMI-FINISHED METALS  Oct 96   Jan/Oct 96	 pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/Sept 95</p>
<p> aluminium		128,805   1,294,661		 -  5.0</p>
<p> copper		   142,660   1,227,719		 -  5.3</p>
<p> zinc			16,655     145,548		 +  4.8</p>
<p> lead			 5,058	39,922		 - 15.2</p>
<p> nickel		     1,788	15,001		 +  3.8</p>
<p> METALS CASTINGS	 Oct 96   Jan/Oct 96	 pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/Sept 95</p>
<p> aluminium		 43,433     401,309		 +  2.0</p>
<p> copper		     6,659	60,182		 - 16.5</p>
<p> zinc			 5,677	53,330		 - 10.4</p>
<p> lead			   539	 5,404		 + 38.1</p>
<p> tin			     27	   200		 - 11.9</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures include alloys. Nickel castings data were not given.</p>
<p>-- Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
